\cf5 \strokec5 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 Chemistry 1015 7 minutes 16 seconds\cb1 \
\cb3 We care a lot about distributions, and we give our distributions different names, because sometimes they exhibit unique properties, and those properties can be generalised into something theoretical. So\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf5 \strokec5 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 Chemistry 1015 7 minutes 36 seconds\cb1 \
\cb3 Do you remember the Excel example I showed where we had a very skewed population? And then I made the sampling distribution out of the sample means. And then I pointed out to you that the sampling distribution was not so skewed. It did not inherit the skewness that was in the underlying population.\cb1 \
